    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. but it feels like the \"smart traffic management\" thing is just a way to delay the inevitable. if we keep pouring money into roads, we're just encouraging more sprawl and more car dependency, which we know is bad for the environment. isn't it basically a losing battle to keep expanding highways when the long-term goal should be moving away from cars entirely?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
